2026-09-17 00:33:47,194 - fhda.data_analysis_env - INFO - Answer: <answer>The distribution of log2 fold changes across all cell type comparisons (excluding PBMCs, covering CD4 vs CD8, CD4 vs CD14, CD4 vs CD19, CD8 vs CD14, CD8 vs CD19, CD14 vs CD19) is approximately symmetric and unimodal, centered at 0 (median = 0, mode = 0, mean ≈ 0.07), with a very sharp central peak and heavy tails — a leptokurtic distribution. The excess kurtosis is extremely high (~16.22, compared to 0 for a normal distribution), skewness is near zero (~0.14), ~85.6% of values fall within [-1, 1], and the tails extend to approximately ±11. This shape is characteristic of a Laplace (double exponential)-like distribution: highly peaked at zero with heavy tails, indicating that most gene comparisons show little or no difference between cell types, while a minority show large fold changes.</answer>
